Streaming Service Features and Functions:
• Login / Welcome Screen for user details to be entered and includes method/s of data security
• Profile Selection - Multiple profiles per account, with age-appropriate content filtering
• Browse / Search - View content library, filter by genre, content type or rating
• Play Content
    o Selecting a title logs it to the profile’s watch history
    o An image of the Movie/TV show appears in place of the functioning video.
    o Do NOT include working video into the project.
• Watchlist - Add or remove titles from the profile’s personal
• Subscription Management - View current plan, upgrade or downgrade plan
• Viewing Report - A .txt file output showing viewing history or a subscription invoice after a change of plan
• Account Credentials - To be its own class within the program which contains:
    o Name, email, password, subscription plan, payment information, list of profiles
    o The Account Credentials file is to be a .csv file.
• GUI – Graphical User Interface made using the CustomTkinter library
    o A logo for the streaming service should be included in the GUI

Object Oriented Programming Requirements:
• Inheritance - A content base class with at least two subclasses (such as Movie and TV Show) sharing attributes and
methods
• Composition - At least one class must contain a collection of other class instances (for example, Account contains a list
of Profile objects)
• Encapsulation - Sensitive attributes (password, payment information) must be protected and accessed through
methods
• Polymorphism - At least one method must be overridden in subclasses with different behaviour (for example, play()
behaves differently for Movie and TV Show)